{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-77830f3ee218c90f","published":"2026-11-24T20:35:47Z","modified":"2026-11-25T15:43:29.649033025Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-23490","CVE-2026-30922","CVE-2026-59884","CVE-2026-59885","CVE-2026-59886","GHSA-63vm-454h-vhhq","GHSA-8ppf-4f7h-5ppj","GHSA-hm4w-wwcw-mr6r","GHSA-jr27-m4p2-rc6r","GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: pyasn1 0.5.0+rhlw.1","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released pyasn1 0.5.0+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-59884, CVE-2026-59886, CVE-2026-30922, CVE-2026-59885, and CVE-2026-23490.\n\nCVE-2026-59884: pyasn1 BER/CER/DER decoder denial of service via unbounded long-form tag IDs\n\nCVE-2026-59886: pyasn1: Uncontrolled resource consumption when converting decoded REAL values\n\nCVE-2026-30922: pyasn1 Vulnerable to Denial of Service via Unbounded Recursion\n\nCVE-2026-59885: pyasn1: Quadratic complexity in OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID processing allows denial of service\n\nCVE-2026-23490: pyasn1 has a DoS vulnerability in decoder\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for pyasn1 0.5.0 from PyPI.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"pyasn1","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:PyPI","purl":"pkg:pypi/pyasn1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0.5.0"},{"fixed":"0.5.0+rhlw.1"}]}],"versions":["0.5.0"],"database_specific":{"lightwell":{"backport_base_version":"0.5.0","remediated_version":"0.5.0+rhlw.1","repository_url":"https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/python/remediated/"},"source":"https://github.com/project-lightwell/lightwell-osv/blob/main/advisories/RHLW-2026-77830f3ee218c90f.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/releases/tag/v0.6.4"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/59xxx/CVE-2026-59884.json"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/pyasn1/pyasn1/security/advisories/GHSA-m4p7-r5rc-7g4j"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-202